ould explain recurring water beneath the drawer. The correct explanation depends on the design of your refrigerator. Clean only accessible areas according to the manual. If water reappears or reaches electrical fittings, arrange an inspection rather than dismantling the appliance."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can you replace a coloured Smeg refrigerator door seal?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "We can assess whether a worn gasket is responsible for poor sealing and check suitable replacement options using your complete model details. The cabinet finish does not determine which gasket fits. Hinge condition and door alignment are also important, particularly if the door is sagging or the sealing surface is damaged."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does Smeg fridge repair require an authorised service centre?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Independent repair may be appropriate for an appliance outside its manufacturer warranty, depending on the fault and available parts. Fridge Repairs Blacktown is not affiliated with Smeg. If your fridge is within warranty or you believe consumer guarantees apply, contact the retailer or manufacturer before commissioning an independent repair."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What should I do if my Smeg fridge clicks repeatedly?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Repeated clicking accompanied by poor cooling can indicate a problem with the starting or control equipment, or the compressor itself. Do not diagnose the component from the noise alone. Move perishables to reliable cold storage, note the sound and book a technician. Avoid repeatedly switching the refrigerator off and on."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Are same-day Smeg fridge repairs available in Western Sydney?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Same-day attendance may be available depending on your location, technician schedule and urgency. An uncommon Smeg component can require a return visit even when diagnosis is completed promptly. Provide the model number and symptoms when booking, and ask us to confirm the available appointment and expected next steps."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I decide whether an old Smeg is worth fixing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Consider the diagnosed fault, the condition of the cabinet, suitable parts availability and the complete repair quote. A sound older cabinet with a minor fault may be worth retaining, especially if its design fits your kitchen. Extensive structural deterioration or an unavailable component can make replacement the more practical choice."}}]}]}</script>", "_css_classes": "frbw"}, "elements": []}]}, {"id": "985f030", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "html_tag": "div", "css_classes": "frb-global-styles frbc"}, "elements": [{"id": "3cac6c5", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "html_tag": "header", "css_classes": "frb-site-header frbc"}, "elements": [{"id": "78930d7", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "html_tag": "div", "css_classes": "frb-header-container frbc"}, "elements": [{"id": "48119a3", "elType": "widget", "settings": {"editor": "<div class="frb-logo">
